Implement `CooldownStore` in cooldown.py: a file-backed record of when each model may be used again.
`CooldownStore(path, clock=time.time)`. Methods: `set(model, until)` stores a unix timestamp (if `until <= clock()` it removes the entry instead);
`active(model) -> bool` (until > now); `remaining(model) -> float` (seconds left, 0.0 if none or expired); `purge() -> int` deletes expired entries and
returns how many were removed. The file is JSON {"model": until}. Requirements: every call re-reads the file (two store objects on one path see
each other's writes); writes are atomic (write a temp file in the same directory then os.replace; no stray temp files are left behind, even if the write fails);
a missing, empty, corrupt or non-object file counts as empty and is overwritten by the next write; entries whose value is not a number (including bool) are ignored.

`python -m unittest` fails in test_paginate.py: the last page is missing and page 1 skips items. Fix `paginate` in paginate.py.
Contract: pages are 1-indexed; "pages" is ceil(len/per_page) (0 for an empty list); a page past the end returns no items; has_next is True when a later page exists;
per_page <= 0 or page < 1 raises ValueError.
